---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href, asset } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout description="Nittany Rover Team is a student-led founding effort at Penn State University Park, bringing together experienced students to develop rovers and pursue careers in space.">
<section class="hero">
<img class="hero-image" src={asset('images/mars-sunrise.webp')} alt="" width="2164" height="727" fetchpriority="high" />
<div class="container hero-content"><h1>Nittany<br />Rover Team</h1><p class="hero-description">A student-led organization bringing together engineering and science to develop rovers—and a community for students pursuing careers in space.</p></div>
</section>
<section id="mission" class="container mission-statement"><div><p class="eyebrow">We are</p><h2>Penn State<br />University Park’s<br />premier space<br />robotics team</h2></div><div class="mission-copy"><p>Nittany Rover Team (NRT) is a student organization at Penn State University Park for students who want to contribute their technical experience to rover development.</p><p>Our aim is to connect mechanical design, electronics, software, and scientific investigation through a shared engineering project. As we develop Project SUNRISE, members will design, build, and test rover systems while documenting what they learn for the students who follow.</p><a class="button" href={href('our-team')}>The Team</a></div></section>
<section class="home-competition"><div class="container"><h2>University<br />Rover Challenge</h2><p>The Mars Society tests student-built rovers in the Utah desert. Penn State University Park participated in the inaugural event in 2007. The team will return in 2028.</p><a class="button" href={href('urc')}>Explore URC</a></div></section>
<section class="container mission-statement"><div class="home-project-title"><h2>Project<br />SUNRISE</h2></div><div class="mission-copy"><p>SUNRISE is our proposed rover. The project will investigate a modular architecture for different mission profiles and payloads, and explore conventional power-generation methods beyond photovoltaic (PV) solar and radioisotope thermoelectric generators (RTGs).</p><p>These concepts remain to be evaluated. Our immediate work is defining requirements and developing the project’s first design direction.</p><a class="button" href={href('projects')}>Explore our projects</a></div></section>
<section class="container recruitment-panel"><h2>Contribute<br />your experience</h2><p>We’re seeking University Park students with experience in mechanical design, electronics, software, or scientific investigation.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={href('join')}>Join Us</a><a class="text-link" href={href('support')}>Support the team</a></div></section>
</Layout>
